        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-miranda-turing-wavelength-s0-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-miranda-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila miranda specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-miranda-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila miranda" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim Bachtrog (2013) measured this wavelength.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the predecessor and successor wavelengths were measured on new specimens in this loop.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Chronoseries wavelengths 1.412 µm (melanogaster) and 2.286 µm (mojavensis) at 0 Ma by D_u ∝ λ².",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities solved so the fastest Schnakenberg mode on a 22.368 µm field is 1.864 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Bachtrog (2013) reviews neo-Y degeneration, including Drosophila miranda. It does not report a 1.9 µm wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg (1979) two-species kinetics used here as the reaction terms.",
        "reported_in_source: Shoup (1966) documents subcellular Drosophila eye pigment granules.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation: a finite band of wavenumbers can grow when the inhibitor out-diffuses the activator.",
        "transfer_boundary: The species-gallery plate is the image-fitness target. It is not an electron micrograph of miranda granules." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila miranda (Neo-X/Neo-Y Sex-Chromosome Evolution Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
